{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445970-is-this-errata-still-small-voice-exceptional-success","id":445970,"title":"Is this errata? Still Small Voice - exceptional success","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T08:39:59-07:00","id":445970,"title":"Is this errata? Still Small Voice - exceptional success","content":"The exceptional success blurb for Still Small Voice (the Wisdom Facet of the Gift of Inspiration on page 127) says that it grants your Wisdom to all rolls to resist Death Rage to all the pack mates that hear you.<br /> <br /> There are rolls to resist Death Rage in this edition? <br /> In looking through that section again, the rolls I saw were to not attack things during Wasu-Im, to gain a few turns worth of lucidity in Wasu-Im, and to resist following your pack mates into Basu-Im when they fall. Now, the third of those is a roll to resist, but the normal success condition for this gift keeps your packmate from slipping from Wasu to Basu, thus contramanding the need for the rest of the rolls (unless someone else happens to be in Wasu-Im at the same time and you don't manage to succeed with Still Small Voice on them).<br /> So my questions here are:<br /> Was there intention for an initial Resolve + Composure roll to resist Wasu-Im when you hit a trigger that got left out of the main Death Rage write up?<br /> Does Still Small Voice help other people who hear it with their lucidity/other actions Resolve + Composure rolls?<br /> OR Was that Exceptional Success effect writen before the initial resistence roll was edited out of the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:13:56-07:00","id":446023,"title":"","content":"When you're in Hard Rage, any Packmates within 10 yards who can see or smell you have to roll Resolve + Composure and fall to Hard Rage if they fail. I'm pretty sure that's the roll Still Small Voice is referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:15:25-07:00","id":446025,"title":"","content":"I'd count it. It's a roll to resist even if it's not a Roll to Resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:46:13-07:00","id":446494,"title":"","content":"I feel like it applies to the Resolve + Composure rolls while in Soft Rage to be lucid (and potentially break out of it) and the ones packmates have to make to resist following a packmate into Hard Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:05:41-07:00","id":446734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445970-is-this-errata-still-small-voice-exceptional-success?p=446494#post446494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it applies to the Resolve + Composure rolls while in Soft Rage to be lucid (and potentially break out of it) and the ones packmates have to make to resist following a packmate into Hard Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes the most sense to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}